# Phase 133 (Visual Atlas Preview) D-07 masking scan: the local pattern-list
# file the scan reads via MASKING_SCAN_PATTERNS_FILE. Repo-root-anchored
# (`/.masking_patterns`, NOT the filesystem root `/`); mirrors the
# PUZZLE_UPLOAD_SECRET env-sourced-secret posture. NEVER commit this file.
/.masking_patterns

# discovery-v3 (2026-08-07): the HMAC key for the NON-DISCLOSING pattern-set
# attestation (`check_atlas_masking.py --attest`). Same handling as
# `.masking_patterns` itself: env-held, gitignored, NOT rotated casually --
# rotating it makes every previously-recorded `pattern_set_hmac` unverifiable,
# which silently downgrades the attestation back to a bare count. An UNKEYED
# attestation deliberately omits all digests (an unkeyed digest is a membership
# oracle: hash a guessed term, compare the prefix).
/.masking_attest_key

# Phase 133 baked atlas asset (offline bake output). Lives OUTSIDE web/static/
# on purpose -- the /static mount at web/main.py:740 serves web/static/
# publicly, which would let the asset bypass the atlas-preview feature flag.
# scp'd to the server like the other sidecar DBs; never committed.
/atlas_data/

# Phase 134 (Discovery Data Spine) built sidecar payload: discovery.db (+ any
# schema-versioned siblings) plus the offline distillation's review/frame
# artifacts. Never commit the built .db -- like the other sidecar DBs
# (pgp.db, fjms_enrichment.db, atlas_data/), it is scp'd to the server /
# bundled with the desktop installer, not tracked in git (DATA-08 deploy
# posture: temp upload -> verify -> atomic rename -> code deploy).
/discovery_data/

# Discovery BUILD depot: the intermediate and candidate artifacts a discovery
# bake produces (reference corpora, match databases, private/public candidate
# sidecars, preview copies, per-run manifests). Relocated here from /_tmp/ on
# 2026-08-16 for one reason: /_tmp/ is this repo's SCRATCH directory -- CLAUDE.md
# and scripts/init.ps1 both describe it as "working notes" and init.ps1 lists its
# contents as ephemera -- and the V4 depot sitting in it included the local twin
# of the artifact production serves, 10.9 GB whose content hash matches its own
# asset_basename. Nothing had deleted it; the point is that clearing scratch is a
# routine act and this was not scratch. Ignored for the same reason as
# /discovery_data/: built payloads are scp'd, never committed. NOTE this is still
# inside the working tree, so `git clean -xfd` would remove it exactly as it
# would /discovery_data/ and /atlas_data/.
/discovery_builds/

# discovery-v3 bake run state (scripts/v3_bake_state.py). Per-run, per-machine
# progress ledgers + their interrupted-write temp files. Already covered by the
# /discovery_data/ and /_tmp/ rules above, but named explicitly and without a
# leading slash so a state file written to ANY directory is ignored: it is
# per-machine run state that must never be committed, and it can carry step
# names and messages. The MODULE and its tests are tracked; only the state it
# emits is not.
v3_bake_state*.json
v3_bake_state*.json.*.tmp
*.bake_state.json
*.bake_state.json.*.tmp

# Ephemeral external-AI (Codex/Gemini) CLI transcripts. These may contain
# restricted M-source/R-source content echoed by the review tool despite
# instructions (confirmed in phase 134 pre-flight rounds r2/r3), so they must
# never be committed -- masking hard constraint. See the project_msource_codename_rule
# memory + .planning/phases/134-discovery-data-spine/deferred-items.md.
tmp/CODEX-*
tmp/codex_*
# 2026-07-24: widened to the whole directory — the CODEX-*/codex_* patterns
# missed same-risk transcripts under other names (135-codex-*-full.log etc.);
# masking leaks recurred here twice. tmp/ is scratch, never committed.
# (tmp/web_deploy_v840.log was untracked in the same commit.)
/tmp/

