# tracked is untracked by this block.

# ACL 2026 reading corpus: ~6,000 downloaded conference PDFs (~24 GB, Tracks/
# alone is 20 GB) plus the 2.2 MB auto-generated paper index and its stray
# "- Copy" duplicate.
# The MARKDOWN NOTE LAYER STAYS TRACKED on purpose — ACL2026-LIBRARY.md,
# RAMBERT-CROSSLINGUAL-EXPERIMENT-PLAN.md, TRACK3-*.md, README.md, and the
# _scan/ + _scan2/ relevance-card sets are the reusable output of the reading
# pass. Do NOT widen this to a bare `ACL2026_papers/`: that would need a
# `git rm --cached` on 21 already-committed notes to have any effect.
ACL2026_papers/Tracks/
ACL2026_papers/Workshops/
ACL2026_papers/Session_*/
ACL2026_papers/Topic_*/
ACL2026_papers/GLOBAL_INDEX.md
ACL2026_papers/GLOBAL_INDEX - Copy.md

# Saved puzzle/join documents sidecar (joins.db + its WAL/SHM).
# NEVER TRACK THIS — it is not merely hygiene, it is a data-loss guard.
# PuzzleService creates the dir and schema at runtime (shared/puzzle_service.py
# mkdir at ~L97), so the repo never needs to supply it; locally it is an empty
# scratch DB. But on the WEB SERVER this same repo-root path holds the LIVE,
# shared, user-created join documents (web/pages/puzzle.py ~L2247), and
# deploy.sh runs `git reset --hard origin/$BRANCH`. reset --hard spares
# untracked/ignored files but clobbers tracked ones — so a committed joins.db
# would wipe every join users saved since that commit, on every deploy.
# (Frozen desktop is unaffected: it uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\GenizahSearchPro\.)
/joins_data/

# PGP raw text dump (~317 MB), sibling of the already-ignored `pgp_data/*.db`
